Cactus Code Thorn Cartoon2DX
Author(s)    : Steven R. Brandt <sbrandt@cct.lsu.edu>
Maintainer(s): Steven R. Brandt <sbrandt@cct.lsu.edu>
Licence      : LGPL (same as SpacetimeX)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

CarpetX port of cactusnumerical/Cartoon2D. Evolves an axisymmetric
system as a thin-in-y Cartesian slab: y-ghosts (and optional x<0
hang-over) are filled by interpolating in cylindrical radius and
rotating tensor components.

Paper: Alcubierre, Brandt, Brügmann, Holz, Seidel, Takahashi,
Thornburg (2001), "Symmetry without symmetry", gr-qc/9908012.
Original cartoon idea: Steve Brandt. Cactus4 Cartoon2D: Sai Iyer.

2. Using this thorn

Activate Cartoon2DX and set the cartoon faces:

  CarpetX::boundary_y       = "cartoon"
  CarpetX::boundary_upper_y = "cartoon"
  CarpetX::boundary_x       = "cartoon"   # half-x: xmin is the axis
  Cartoon2DX::fill_negative_x = yes
  CarpetX::ncells_y = 1                   # one cell; y=0 at the centre

Tag grid-function groups with tensortypealias (Scalar / U / DD_sym),
or rely on an existing parities tag. No glue thorn is required.

See doc/documentation.tex for the algorithm, grid layout, and
parameter notes.

3. Tests

  test/tov.par                 Cactus testsuite: low-res TOV, 2 steps
  test/standalone_math_test.cxx  g++ test of the interpolation/rotation math
  Docs/thornlist/cartoon2dx.th   GetComponents list for this feature
